<title>UK: Exeter Investment Group shares set premium.</title>
<headline>Exeter Investment Group shares set premium.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Exeter Investment Group Plc set a modest premium on their first day trading on the London Stock Exchange's Alternative Investment Market on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The shares were quoted at 97-1/2p by 0900 GMT, compared with a placing price of 92p, although no trade was recorded.</p>
<p>At the placing price the Exeter-based investment management group was valued at 8.74 million stg.</p>
<p>The float, sponsored by Greig Middleton, raised 3.9 million stg including 1.15 million stg of new money, which will fund investment and reduce borrowings.</p>
<p>-- John Sutherland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7945</p>
